The shipped function-granular RAM text list (perf-plan 2026-09-23 C39).

agg-hot.list: 137 flash-text functions, 24,320 B, chosen by hart-1 PC samples
per byte over Doom + Quake + the SDL canary on kernel #358 (idle excluded),
built with FASTFN=patches/0062-esp32s31-fastfn-list/agg-hot.list (the Makefile
default). Measured on fresh boots against #358: same-hart pingpong 342/330/333
vs 466-484 us (-29%), Quake 21.3/21.6 vs 20.0/20.1 fps, gate 22/22.
agg-cold.list: the same-size layout control (182 zero-sample functions from the
same objects): pingpong 404 (-14%, layout), Quake 18.5/19.7 (no gain). The
Quake gain is the functions; about half the pingpong gain is packing.

Regenerate after a layout change with scripts/board/fastfn-pick.py from fresh
profile-apps.sh captures resolved against `nm -nS vmlinux` of the kernel they
were taken on; verify with scripts/board/fastfn-verify.py after the build.
